== Tips ==

* After obtaining all items that cost {{Item|Green Candy}}, spending the excess into '''Bat Fireworks''' is a good idea to "convert" them into an average of {{Green|11}} {{Item|Purple Candy}} per '''Bat Firework'''.
* The {{green|30}} seconds cooldown can be circumvented by swapping lobbies via the {{NPCSprite|Hub Selector}}.

== Trivia ==
*Bat Fireworks used to directly put Candy directly into the player's inventory rather than drop them.
*The player who launches it must have a {{Item|Trick or Treat Bag}}, {{Item|Spooky Sack}} or {{Item|Events Sack}} in their inventory or [[Sack of Sacks]].
*Although Bat Fireworks can only be spawned in the {{Zone|Village}}, the bats themselves can travel all around the {{Zone|The Hub}}.
*A player can only collect up to {{Item|Green Candy|amount=25}} from each firework no matter who launches it.
*The candies collected from the {{Item|Bat Piñata}}s do not count towards the score in the [[Spooky Festival]].

